# The CDN-vs-GitHub reconcile ledger: one line per version published with no release to audit
# against, and DELIBERATELY MACHINE-LOCAL (scripts/lib/release-lib.sh says so where it defines
# the path). `git add -A` swept it into the 1.2.450 release commit on 2026-09-22, which put a
# live debt into every checkout and made `scripts/test/publish-release.bash` fail in CI — its
# scenarios got the reconcile refusal where they expect the stale-exe one. Ignored so the next
# `git add -A` cannot do it again.
docs/agents/release-reconcile.txt
